WEBVTT

00:00:06.177 --> 00:00:11.687
I share my unstoppable curiosity with you.

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:17.487
I'm still able to run through the fog...

00:00:17.587 --> 00:00:21.177
...because I know that you're here for me.

00:00:21.277 --> 00:00:28.907
I guess the shape of happiness is different for everyone...

00:00:28.907 --> 00:00:33.247
...however, I know it's boring when I'm alone...

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:35.127
But, with you...

00:00:35.127 --> 00:00:37.207
...it's like a mystery!

00:00:39.047 --> 00:00:42.797
It's an enchanting future, where...

00:00:42.967 --> 00:00:47.517
...in order for me to be strong, it's always you...

00:00:47.517 --> 00:00:51.897
...that I can continue to depend on, right?

00:00:51.897 --> 00:00:53.477
Just to survive!

00:00:53.647 --> 00:00:55.437
Stumped Q? Don't lose your way!

00:00:55.437 --> 00:00:57.277
Take this moment...

00:00:57.277 --> 00:01:00.897
...to fix your gaze and charge on ahead!

00:01:00.897 --> 00:01:03.107
Eternally, we'll always be together...

00:01:03.107 --> 00:01:04.947
...searching and pursuing...

00:01:04.947 --> 00:01:08.657
...the meaning of it all.

00:01:08.657 --> 00:01:10.787
Truth is nothing but a labyrinth...

00:01:10.787 --> 00:01:12.497
...that we try to continue through...

00:01:12.497 --> 00:01:16.167
...especially when we are hurt.

00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:18.337
I'll take you, so come this way.

00:01:18.337 --> 00:01:20.167
I'm certain that, on that day...

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:24.087
...I'll see your smile, face to face!

00:01:32.303 --> 00:01:35.606
Attend a detective school? I'll never permit it!

00:01:35.707 --> 00:01:36.908
Why?

00:01:37.175 --> 00:01:39.310
I've wanted to be a detective for such along time!

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:41.345
Dreams and reality are two different things!

00:01:41.379 --> 00:01:43.748
At least let me see if I can get in.

00:01:43.848 --> 00:01:46.150
I'll really, really study more for school, so please!

00:01:46.451 --> 00:01:49.821
Kyuu, you don't even know what
kind of work a detective does.

00:01:50.488 --> 00:01:53.224
It's constantly dangerous and disruptive!

00:01:53.558 --> 00:01:56.594
It's not the same as those Sherlock Holmes
videos you're always watching.

00:01:56.928 --> 00:01:58.930
I understand that…

00:01:59.063 --> 00:02:00.665
You don't understand!

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.135
If you only knew…

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:06.804
Mom?

00:02:08.639 --> 00:02:10.641
In any case, I definitely won't permit it.

00:02:10.708 --> 00:02:12.510
Hurry up and go to school.

00:02:12.844 --> 00:02:14.178
I'm going now…

00:02:24.422 --> 00:02:25.690
Sorry, mom…

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:27.258
I'm going anyway.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.602
This place…

00:02:37.869 --> 00:02:40.071
It's sort of like a concert hall.

00:02:40.404 --> 00:02:41.672
Kyuu!

00:02:44.342 --> 00:02:47.979
Mega! Kintarou! You guys really came!

00:02:47.979 --> 00:02:48.913
Of course!

00:02:49.447 --> 00:02:52.750
But, could you not call me Kintarou?
I'm not a piece of candy.

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:54.285
Golden Boy Candy?

00:02:54.786 --> 00:02:56.854
Call me Kinta-san. Kinta-san.

00:02:57.121 --> 00:02:58.823
Well then, Kinta it is.

00:02:59.157 --> 00:03:02.393
Heh, that's yobisute, you know. Well, never-mind.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:04.395
So all three of us came.

00:03:04.562 --> 00:03:05.163
Yeah.

00:03:05.496 --> 00:03:07.732
Now then, shall we head into the hall then?

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.501
We'll definitely pass!

00:03:10.501 --> 00:03:11.269
Let's do it!

00:03:11.369 --> 00:03:12.203
Yeah!

00:03:14.939 --> 00:03:18.442
He's the one you're calling a diamond in the rough?

00:03:19.043 --> 00:03:19.610
Yes.

00:03:20.711 --> 00:03:22.180
This should be fun.

00:03:25.349 --> 00:03:27.218
Wow, there's so many people.

00:03:27.919 --> 00:03:31.022
All these people are applying to
the Dan Detective Academy!

00:03:31.823 --> 00:03:33.291
More than I expected.

00:03:33.624 --> 00:03:34.592
You expected?

00:03:35.259 --> 00:03:36.994
It's like Shine-san said, isn't it?

00:03:37.295 --> 00:03:40.998
Even the police have complete
confidence in this academy.

00:03:41.532 --> 00:03:45.736
They often ask the school to help
investigate and solve big cases.

00:03:46.003 --> 00:03:46.671
Yeah.

00:03:46.804 --> 00:03:50.107
As a result, every year thousands of people
come here to take the entrance test…

00:03:50.107 --> 00:03:52.310
…but only a handful actually pass.

00:03:52.844 --> 00:03:57.381
There are many different geniuses here. They say
there are even professional detectives here too!

00:03:57.481 --> 00:03:58.516
That's exactly right.

00:03:58.983 --> 00:04:02.486
DDS is the only school in Japan where
students are allowed to bear arms.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:07.291
After all, the legendary detective, Dan Morihiko,
created this technical academy!

00:04:07.859 --> 00:04:10.862
So you're saying it won't be easy to pass?

00:04:11.028 --> 00:04:11.963
That's right.

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:13.865
No time to be absent-minded.

00:04:14.198 --> 00:04:16.500
This is bad. What am I going to do?

00:04:16.801 --> 00:04:19.070
What's this? Have you given up already?

00:04:19.337 --> 00:04:20.838
No.

00:04:20.938 --> 00:04:26.544
Even though it sounds so difficult, I'm getting
excited. This school is really terrific!

00:04:26.711 --> 00:04:27.378
Huh?

00:04:28.012 --> 00:04:29.447
He has strange reactions.

00:04:29.847 --> 00:04:31.849
Ah! If it isn't Megumi-chan.

00:04:32.884 --> 00:04:34.051
Saburoumaru-san!

00:04:34.418 --> 00:04:35.086
Yo!

00:04:35.586 --> 00:04:37.088
Are you going to take the test too?

00:04:37.355 --> 00:04:39.991
I don't really plan to become a detective.

00:04:40.091 --> 00:04:41.859
But it's a good way to test my unique skills.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:46.998
You see, if I am accepted to DDS
it might bring me a bit of fame.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:50.768
He's the same irritating guy as always.

00:04:51.002 --> 00:04:57.875
But, when my rival has a photographic memory, I'll
have to stay on my toes even though my IQ is 180.

00:04:58.175 --> 00:04:58.709
See ya.

00:05:00.444 --> 00:05:02.346
Do you know that guy?

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:08.019
Yeah. He goes to the Ability Development
Institute, the same as I do.

00:05:08.586 --> 00:05:12.323
He's Saburoumaru Yutaka-san. He's already
been accepted by Tokyo University.

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:14.659
Ah… Tokyo University?

00:05:15.226 --> 00:05:16.427
He must be real smart then…

00:05:17.028 --> 00:05:22.066
He might be smart, but man, Tokyo University
students are pretty annoying.

00:05:22.333 --> 00:05:23.601
They sure are.

00:05:25.069 --> 00:05:27.505
Hey, there are elementary school students here too?

00:05:28.039 --> 00:05:29.006
Really?

00:05:29.307 --> 00:05:30.408
Maybe he got lost?

00:05:30.908 --> 00:05:32.610
Eh? That boy!

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:33.844
Do you know him?

00:05:34.578 --> 00:05:37.348
He's the genius programmer,
Narusawa Kazuma-kun.

00:05:38.549 --> 00:05:39.417
Genius…

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:40.818
…programmer.

00:05:41.419 --> 00:05:46.557
He's the genius who, when he was still in the fifth
grade, created some really popular games.

00:05:46.791 --> 00:05:49.894
Ever played a game called 'The
Case Files of Young Kibarashi'?

00:05:50.695 --> 00:05:51.662
I know that game!

00:05:51.896 --> 00:05:54.465
He's just one of the many geniuses gathered here.

00:06:03.207 --> 00:06:04.475
It's Shino-san…

00:06:05.509 --> 00:06:10.948
Attention all candidates, we will now
commence with the first exam.

00:06:11.349 --> 00:06:13.484
Please look carefully at the screen in front of you.

00:06:24.095 --> 00:06:25.529
What's with this picture?

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:27.331
What is that for?

00:06:27.865 --> 00:06:30.134
What does this mean, Kyuu?

00:06:35.339 --> 00:06:37.908
Why is Kyuu so serious all of a sudden?

00:06:41.979 --> 00:06:46.183
The picture you just saw was, in
fact, from a real homicide case.

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:49.253
The only clue we have was this
picture from the crime scene.

00:06:49.987 --> 00:06:51.989
Oh crap! So that's what it was.

00:06:52.456 --> 00:06:55.726
Immediately after the culprit left the scene…

00:06:55.726 --> 00:06:59.296
…the victim used the last of his
strength to take this snapshot.

00:07:00.297 --> 00:07:05.870
Candidates, you are to deduce the real murderer
from the hints in the picture you just saw.

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:07.605
So that's it.

00:07:08.172 --> 00:07:12.076
Anyone who assumed that picture was just an
ordinary room and didn't pay attention to it…

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:14.478
…isn't qualified to be a detective.

00:07:15.046 --> 00:07:19.717
The room in which the crime occurred
is in this cottage at the edge of a lake.

00:07:20.651 --> 00:07:25.456
This is the site as it was photographed by the
police after the incident was detected.

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:28.859
The victim was a photographer, Fushimi Kenzou.

00:07:28.893 --> 00:07:31.128
Twenty-eight years old and a first-dan in judo.

00:07:31.562 --> 00:07:36.367
He had come to photograph the lake during
January where the cold temperatures…

00:07:36.367 --> 00:07:38.536
…were still ten degrees below freezing.

00:07:39.336 --> 00:07:44.909
His corpse was discovered lying on the
bed on January 20… at 10:15 am.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:48.512
Death was caused by stabbing
with a sharp-edged knife.

00:07:48.612 --> 00:07:51.148
The estimated time of death was 1:00 a.m.

00:07:51.749 --> 00:07:55.586
Because death was not immediate, in
the few moments before he died…

00:07:55.719 --> 00:07:59.256
…we believe he took the photograph
you were shown at first.

00:07:59.957 --> 00:08:05.229
The criminal left the scene at first but later returned in order to destroy evidence.

00:08:05.463 --> 00:08:06.097
Eh?

00:08:06.597 --> 00:08:12.770
Ah, you see, in the first picture taken by the
victim, the ashtray had fallen to the floor.

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:15.106
That's a sign that there was a small struggle.

00:08:15.339 --> 00:08:19.009
But in the police's picture of the scene,
it had been completely cleared away.

00:08:19.143 --> 00:08:20.411
That's true.

00:08:21.145 --> 00:08:23.914
Based on the hints we have
up to now, we can deduce…

00:08:28.519 --> 00:08:34.125
After stabbing the victim, the criminal panicked and
fled the room without seeing if he was dead.

00:08:34.959 --> 00:08:38.596
Then he came back later in order
to destroy the evidence.

00:08:38.996 --> 00:08:44.368
That means something within that first picture
could possibly tell us the killer's identity.

00:08:44.368 --> 00:08:46.537
It was the victim's 'dying message'.

00:08:48.572 --> 00:08:50.341
Kyuu is really incredible.

00:08:52.209 --> 00:08:53.077
Wait a moment.

00:08:53.544 --> 00:08:55.079
Did you think of something else?

00:08:55.846 --> 00:08:59.049
Maybe the right term is 'dining'
message? Or is it 'diving'?

00:09:00.551 --> 00:09:03.721
Dining is eating a meal. Diving is plunging down.

00:09:04.722 --> 00:09:06.590
Oops, spoke too soon.

00:09:13.564 --> 00:09:14.999
Who are these people?

00:09:15.866 --> 00:09:19.770
The six people currently assembled on the
stage are part of our academy's staff.

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:21.372
They're the suspects for this case.

00:09:21.672 --> 00:09:22.540
Suspects?

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:24.475
The culprit is among these people.

00:09:24.808 --> 00:09:27.411
But, why is a cactus there?

00:09:28.145 --> 00:09:32.917
These six people were guests from the Lakeside
Hotel, two kilometers from the crime scene.

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:36.387
Each person has a motive and has no alibi.

00:09:36.787 --> 00:09:40.090
As you can see, three of them have injuries.

00:09:40.357 --> 00:09:45.196
Each one has testified that they had a small
accident on the day of the murder.

00:09:45.663 --> 00:09:47.998
Number one is a left handed woman.

00:09:49.133 --> 00:09:51.468
You see, she's wearing her watch on her right wrist.

00:09:51.702 --> 00:09:54.438
Number two is an old man whose
right hand is injured.

00:09:54.905 --> 00:09:58.008
Number three is a man whose ankle
is wrapped with bandages.

00:09:58.475 --> 00:10:01.979
Number four looks like a student
who's wearing an eye patch.

00:10:02.479 --> 00:10:04.448
In any case, it's not number five.

00:10:04.882 --> 00:10:08.652
No matter how strong the old man is, it's not
possible for him to kill a first-dan in judo.

00:10:09.453 --> 00:10:11.789
Number six, the cactus, is out of the question.

00:10:13.324 --> 00:10:15.793
I've already figured out who the real criminal is!

00:10:16.126 --> 00:10:16.794
No way!

00:10:17.328 --> 00:10:18.929
I've decided too.

00:10:19.263 --> 00:10:20.998
You already decided?

00:10:22.166 --> 00:10:23.534
Yes, using these!

00:10:24.368 --> 00:10:25.536
Dice?

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:27.871
You decided that way?

00:10:28.439 --> 00:10:33.310
Starting now the six suspects will leave the hall
and head towards various destinations.

00:10:33.711 --> 00:10:37.448
Candidates, please follow the suspect
that you deduce to be the murderer.

00:10:37.648 --> 00:10:41.318
Please find out their destination before 3:00 pm.

00:10:41.885 --> 00:10:45.723
If you can't discover the real culprit, we won't
permit you to attempt the second test.

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:49.493
So first they are challenging our deduction
and surveillance abilities.

00:10:49.727 --> 00:10:51.462
The suspects are leaving one by one.

00:10:51.895 --> 00:10:53.998
No! I can't get nervous or else
I won't be able to think

00:10:54.298 --> 00:10:54.965
Megu…

00:10:55.666 --> 00:10:57.001
It's this way…

00:10:57.468 --> 00:10:58.135
The culprit is…

00:10:58.135 --> 00:10:59.370
No! Don't tell me!

00:10:59.937 --> 00:11:00.671
Why not?

00:11:00.904 --> 00:11:04.275
If I depend on others for something like
this, then I am not fit to be a detective.

00:11:04.842 --> 00:11:06.644
I should find out the answers on my own.

00:11:08.312 --> 00:11:11.315
Sorry. Just one hint then.

00:11:12.116 --> 00:11:20.391
The answer to this problem is what
you didn't see in the picture.

00:11:23.594 --> 00:11:24.261
That's it!

00:11:24.595 --> 00:11:25.696
I know now, Kyuu.

00:11:26.530 --> 00:11:28.165
The culprit is person number three!

00:11:30.301 --> 00:11:33.270
Hey! My dice have made my decision for me.

00:11:33.871 --> 00:11:35.639
Kinta, what did your dice decide?

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:39.743
Same answer. My dice came up number three.

00:11:40.177 --> 00:11:41.111
So we've all decided.

00:11:41.312 --> 00:11:41.812
Yep!

00:11:44.848 --> 00:11:49.720
As long as I follow the girl with the photographic
memory, there's no way I'll be wrong.

00:11:50.654 --> 00:11:53.357
There's more than one way to win this match

00:11:55.326 --> 00:11:58.062
Like you said, nobody chose the cactus.

00:11:58.629 --> 00:12:04.802
Of course not. No matter how much the they might
need a disguise, no one would choose a cactus.

00:12:05.235 --> 00:12:09.139
Oh? You just don't understand the
finer points of this disguise.

00:12:10.307 --> 00:12:13.377
Well, leave the rest to me, Nanami Koutarou.

00:12:13.977 --> 00:12:14.845
Please.

00:12:15.579 --> 00:12:17.214
But no more cactus, okay?

00:12:34.498 --> 00:12:35.532
He went up.

00:12:35.599 --> 00:12:36.433
Hey. Let's go.

00:12:36.667 --> 00:12:37.134
Yeah.

00:12:46.477 --> 00:12:47.111
Eh?

00:12:47.878 --> 00:12:49.146
Where did he go?

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:50.781
This way!

00:12:51.615 --> 00:12:54.885
That man wearing a jacket.
He was the number three man.

00:12:55.219 --> 00:12:55.819
What?

00:12:56.387 --> 00:12:58.622
He was wearing the same watch!

00:12:58.889 --> 00:13:01.225
The only difference is that he's
wearing his jacket inside-out!

00:13:01.725 --> 00:13:03.827
Jacket? That's it!

00:13:04.128 --> 00:13:06.330
Kyuu, this repays my debt from before.

00:13:06.663 --> 00:13:08.565
That's instant photographic memory for you!

00:13:08.932 --> 00:13:11.268
What's that? Instant teakettle skill?

00:13:12.503 --> 00:13:16.507
This is Nanami. So far ten people
have passed the first point.

00:13:22.312 --> 00:13:23.781
I wonder where he's going?

00:13:23.914 --> 00:13:26.216
He bought a ticket for 640 yen.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:29.019
Eh? You can see that far, Kinta?

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:32.790
Of course, my eyesight is 20/20.

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:34.858
But your eyes are so small.

00:13:34.958 --> 00:13:37.094
It has nothing to do with the size of my eyes!

00:13:37.461 --> 00:13:38.862
Let's buy tickets too.

00:13:38.962 --> 00:13:39.696
Okay.

00:13:41.398 --> 00:13:45.669
Mega, has your photographic
memory memorized this map?

00:13:46.103 --> 00:13:49.072
I guess, it's all somewhere in my head.

00:13:49.339 --> 00:13:49.740
Good.

00:13:50.007 --> 00:13:52.609
You are really great. So this is your
photographic memory trick?

00:13:52.676 --> 00:13:55.779
That's wrong! It's not a trick! It's an ability!

00:13:56.180 --> 00:13:56.747
Shall we go?

00:13:57.114 --> 00:13:58.582
Hey, wait for me.

00:13:58.916 --> 00:14:00.551
Hmm. Ticket… Ticket…

00:14:01.084 --> 00:14:02.786
Eh? Where's my wallet?

00:14:03.253 --> 00:14:05.756
The train is an express to Kitakaze.

00:14:06.356 --> 00:14:08.058
Express to Kitakaze.

00:14:08.826 --> 00:14:11.128
Please take care not to board the wrong train.

00:14:12.129 --> 00:14:13.363
We have to get on the train!

00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:14.264
Hold on.

00:14:17.668 --> 00:14:18.602
Wait here.

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:23.407
What do you mean? He's on this train!

00:14:23.607 --> 00:14:26.643
l f we lose track of him here we'll be disqualified!

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:28.045
Trust me!

00:15:06.283 --> 00:15:07.418
Oh, well.

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:10.955
It's gone.

00:15:11.689 --> 00:15:13.491
Have we been eliminated then?

00:15:14.191 --> 00:15:14.825
Nope.

00:15:15.426 --> 00:15:17.261
We're safe, Megu.

00:15:17.428 --> 00:15:18.129
Huh?

00:15:19.397 --> 00:15:20.131
Ah!

00:15:21.265 --> 00:15:22.033
Hey!

00:15:22.433 --> 00:15:23.501
Where is that guy?

00:15:24.668 --> 00:15:25.970
Kinta, where were you?

00:15:27.772 --> 00:15:30.141
Geez, I lost my wallet and my money.

00:15:30.741 --> 00:15:32.476
I'm late because I was looking for it.

00:15:34.178 --> 00:15:35.479
You're a lucky guy.

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:36.580
Huh?

00:15:41.085 --> 00:15:42.820
Man number three isn't here.

00:15:43.821 --> 00:15:45.189
What happened…

00:15:45.556 --> 00:15:47.725
What's more, Megu and the
others aren't here either.

00:15:48.192 --> 00:15:53.764
HEY, EVERYONE! WHERE DID YOU GO? WHERE?

00:15:56.133 --> 00:15:57.735
He didn't get on the train?

00:15:58.402 --> 00:15:58.869
No.

00:15:59.303 --> 00:16:01.172
Let's hurry over to the opposite platform.

00:16:01.539 --> 00:16:01.939
Okay.

00:16:07.778 --> 00:16:11.215
But, how did you know that he
wouldn't take the train?

00:16:11.649 --> 00:16:13.984
That is all because of you two, Megu and Kinta.

00:16:14.118 --> 00:16:14.518
Eh?

00:16:14.618 --> 00:16:15.252
Us?

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:17.822
The train that left just now is an express.

00:16:18.155 --> 00:16:20.391
It won't stop before it reaches the
final station at Kitakazedai.

00:16:21.182 --> 00:16:23.918
If he wanted to get off at the Kitakazedai station…

00:16:24.219 --> 00:16:26.087
…then 240 yen would have been enough.

00:16:26.988 --> 00:16:30.258
However, he bought a ticket for 640 yen.

00:16:30.658 --> 00:16:31.593
Don't you think that's strange?

00:16:31.893 --> 00:16:32.660
Sure is.

00:16:33.094 --> 00:16:35.430
Eh? That's not too bad.

00:16:36.331 --> 00:16:39.567
In fact, he really intended to
take a different train, right?

00:16:39.868 --> 00:16:41.336
Isn't that what you're thinking?

00:16:42.670 --> 00:16:45.306
You're the genius pro-bowler,
Narusawa Kazuma-kun!

00:16:46.975 --> 00:16:47.475
Huh?

00:16:48.343 --> 00:16:49.711
Programmer!

00:16:49.911 --> 00:16:53.915
Oh, that's right. The genius
programmer, Kazuma-kun.

00:16:54.282 --> 00:16:55.783
You didn't take that train either.

00:16:57.051 --> 00:17:00.288
I have researched everyone's
data using the internet.

00:17:01.856 --> 00:17:04.726
A member of the National Ability
Development Institute…

00:17:04.726 --> 00:17:07.729
…blessed with a photographic
memory, Minami Megumi-san.

00:17:08.830 --> 00:17:11.766
Called the master of sight, the descendent
of that Touyama Kinshiro…

00:17:12.100 --> 00:17:15.870
…who was later known as Touyama
no Kin-san, Touyama Kintarou-san.

00:17:16.371 --> 00:17:20.008
Touyama no Kin-san? The one with the sakura
snowstorm tattooed on his back?

00:17:20.508 --> 00:17:22.010
Is that so?

00:17:22.210 --> 00:17:23.478
It's really nothing.

00:17:24.479 --> 00:17:25.180
But…

00:17:27.048 --> 00:17:30.151
There were no hits for your data, oniisan.

00:17:31.052 --> 00:17:33.788
None of the search engins: I used had anything.

00:17:37.992 --> 00:17:40.395
I'm Kyuu. Nice to meet you, Kazuma-kun.

00:17:40.662 --> 00:17:42.330
A-Ah. Yes. Yes.

00:17:46.501 --> 00:17:48.503
Hey, looks like he's getting on this time.

00:17:49.871 --> 00:17:54.042
With 640 yen, his destination would
be the Minamiyama Nature Park.

00:17:54.475 --> 00:17:55.610
Alright then, let's go!

00:18:01.549 --> 00:18:03.518
We've got some incredible members, don't we?

00:18:03.851 --> 00:18:08.389
Memory genius Minami Megumi and genius
programmer Narusawa Kazuma.

00:18:09.023 --> 00:18:11.159
And moreover, genius eye Touya...

00:18:11.159 --> 00:18:11.426
Quiet!

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:13.394
What did you hit me for?

00:18:13.628 --> 00:18:15.163
Stop talking nonsense!

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:17.232
But it's the truth!

00:18:17.265 --> 00:18:18.299
What?

00:18:18.366 --> 00:18:19.400
Now, now.

00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:22.937
But, Kyuu…

00:18:23.972 --> 00:18:26.441
Why is number three the culprit?

00:18:27.342 --> 00:18:30.478
You didn't see anything except for
the pictures shown on the screen…

00:18:30.778 --> 00:18:32.914
But you figured out the culprit right away?

00:18:33.615 --> 00:18:37.318
Where in that picture was the evidence
which makes him the culprit?

00:18:37.719 --> 00:18:40.521
I didn't figure it out from what I saw.

00:18:40.888 --> 00:18:43.224
It was something that wasn't
there that gave it away.

00:18:43.358 --> 00:18:44.525
Something that wasn't there?

00:18:45.059 --> 00:18:45.526
Yup.

00:18:47.028 --> 00:18:50.665
If the criminal had left any of
his personal things there…

00:18:51.299 --> 00:18:53.134
…the victim ought to have photographed them.

00:18:54.002 --> 00:18:57.272
Still, no matter how we look at that picture,
there isn't anything like that.

00:18:58.640 --> 00:19:01.142
Therefore, I reversed my thinking.

00:19:01.609 --> 00:19:02.277
Reversed?

00:19:02.877 --> 00:19:07.382
The culprit must not have left any
evidence in the first place.

00:19:07.615 --> 00:19:08.549
Wait a moment.

00:19:09.017 --> 00:19:12.520
If he didn't come to destroy evidence,
why did the culprit bother to return?

00:19:13.087 --> 00:19:17.025
Therefore we reverse our thinking.
That's why Kyuu gave me that hint.

00:19:17.425 --> 00:19:20.795
The answer to this problem is what
you didn't see in the picture.

00:19:21.663 --> 00:19:22.397
That's it, right?

00:19:22.664 --> 00:19:23.298
Yeah.

00:19:24.032 --> 00:19:28.770
The culprit didn't come back to remove
evidence. He came to plant it!

00:19:28.970 --> 00:19:29.871
Plant it?

00:19:30.838 --> 00:19:31.706
Have a look.

00:19:32.006 --> 00:19:32.540
Huh?

00:19:34.742 --> 00:19:36.644
Ah, Kazuma-kun. When did you do this?

00:19:36.811 --> 00:19:38.379
You have to make use of whatever you can.

00:19:44.118 --> 00:19:44.786
Hold on a moment.

00:19:45.453 --> 00:19:47.689
This is the picture that was taken by the victim.

00:19:50.725 --> 00:19:53.061
And this picture was taken by the police.

00:19:54.662 --> 00:19:56.497
I understand now! It's the shoes.

00:19:57.165 --> 00:19:59.400
There's a pair of shoes in the
picture taken by the police.

00:19:59.834 --> 00:20:02.203
But they're not in the picture taken by the victim!

00:20:02.403 --> 00:20:05.740
Naturally they aren't the shoes of
the culprit who had already left.

00:20:05.807 --> 00:20:08.509
Why do you think the victim's
shoes wouldn't be there?

00:20:09.677 --> 00:20:11.612
You mean the culprit wore them?

00:20:12.113 --> 00:20:13.014
That's right!

00:20:13.648 --> 00:20:16.951
The victim took the picture in order to show that.

00:20:17.919 --> 00:20:21.189
But, why did the culprit bother
to wear the victim's shoes?

00:20:22.123 --> 00:20:25.393
He wouldn't have come in bare feet in that cold
weather, ten degrees below freezing…

00:20:26.127 --> 00:20:27.328
There are two hints!

00:20:28.629 --> 00:20:32.066
The first is that the crime scene
was at the edge of the lake.

00:20:33.167 --> 00:20:38.039
The other is that it had been ten degrees
below freezing for a while.

00:20:40.241 --> 00:20:42.377
Damn it! I don't understand at all.

00:20:42.577 --> 00:20:45.513
Why in the world would the culprit
not be wearing shoes?

00:20:47.315 --> 00:20:48.549
There's only one answer!

00:20:48.883 --> 00:20:50.051
That's right, only one.

00:20:50.618 --> 00:20:52.053
Ice skates, right?

00:20:52.253 --> 00:20:53.020
Exactly!

00:20:53.421 --> 00:20:54.789
Ice skates?

00:20:56.257 --> 00:21:01.129
The hotel where the culprit was staying and the
victim's cottage are both on the same lake.

00:21:01.963 --> 00:21:04.465
Rather than walking around the lake…

00:21:04.599 --> 00:21:07.668
…the culprit used skates to cross the
lake directly to the crime scene.

00:21:08.669 --> 00:21:13.508
Probably he thought that way was faster and less
conspicuous than walking during the night.

00:21:14.342 --> 00:21:18.880
However, as he was committing the crime, the
victim, who was a first-dan in judo, threw him.

00:21:20.848 --> 00:21:22.884
And he sprained his ankle.

00:21:23.484 --> 00:21:25.586
He couldn't skate with a sprained ankle.

00:21:25.920 --> 00:21:28.689
But, other than the skates, the culprit
didn't have any other shoes.

00:21:31.726 --> 00:21:34.862
So the criminal wore the victim's shoes and fled.

00:21:37.398 --> 00:21:40.835
And then the criminal came back
and returned the shoes he took.

00:21:41.536 --> 00:21:44.238
If the shoes were missing, that would
be suspicious, wouldn't it?

00:21:44.605 --> 00:21:46.707
So that's it. That's what happened.

00:21:47.408 --> 00:21:49.811
Yes, and since there is only one culprit…

00:21:50.578 --> 00:21:54.549
And since among the six people, the only one who
couldn't skate on the day of the incident was…

00:21:54.982 --> 00:21:58.586
Number three, the man who had the injured ankle.

00:22:01.622 --> 00:22:03.024
I see now.

00:22:03.691 --> 00:22:07.328
Kyuu, you're really good at thinking fast and far.

00:22:07.895 --> 00:22:08.996
Indeed.

00:22:09.230 --> 00:22:11.966
Not bad for someone I haven't any data on.

00:22:12.300 --> 00:22:15.770
It's kind of embarrassing to be
praised by true geniuses.

00:22:17.572 --> 00:22:19.073
Thank you for riding with us.

00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:21.609
This next stop is the Minamiyama Nature Park.

00:22:21.609 --> 00:22:23.611
Minamiyama Nature Park is the next stop.

00:22:30.351 --> 00:22:31.185
He got off.

00:22:31.586 --> 00:22:32.186
Alright!

00:22:35.690 --> 00:22:41.128
Hey, is the second exam really going
to be in a wild place like this?

00:22:41.596 --> 00:22:43.364
Looks like an unmanned station too.

00:22:43.865 --> 00:22:47.435
No problem. There's no mistake that he's the culprit.

00:22:47.835 --> 00:22:49.303
In any case, let's follow him.

00:22:49.704 --> 00:22:51.806
It would be bad to lose him after coming this far.

00:22:52.039 --> 00:22:52.840
Sure would.

00:22:56.310 --> 00:22:57.512
Begin tailing!

00:22:59.847 --> 00:23:01.682
Why does everyone have have to run?

00:23:04.151 --> 00:23:07.722
This is Nanami. Four people have
reached the second point.

00:23:10.691 --> 00:23:15.997
Damn it! I, Saburoumaru, won't be left
behind! This match is far from over!!

00:23:16.364 --> 00:23:19.600
Correction, five people have
reached the second point.

00:23:20.701 --> 00:23:24.205
Well now, I wonder if any will qualify this year.

00:23:28.009 --> 00:23:31.846
Sorry mom, but I'm definitely going to pass!

00:23:36.456 --> 00:23:46.706
Unable to cry in front of you, I'm whistling instead.

00:23:50.096 --> 00:24:01.306
Saying I'll always be beside you without saying a single word.

00:24:01.546 --> 00:24:08.636
My loving heart is overflowing; those sad thoughts...

00:24:08.636 --> 00:24:14.266
are like things that fade away unnoticed in mid-air.

00:24:14.466 --> 00:24:20.376
And again, with a mighty smile of relief...

00:24:20.476 --> 00:24:25.926
I will see you off.

00:24:26.176 --> 00:24:35.366
Goodbye and thank you.

00:24:38.277 --> 00:24:39.778
On the way to the second exam center…

00:24:40.079 --> 00:24:42.014
…we found ourselves in the middle of a forest.

00:24:42.515 --> 00:24:44.483
We encountered trap after trap.

00:24:45.050 --> 00:24:46.619
I got separated from the others and now I'm alone!

00:24:46.919 --> 00:24:49.054
This is where a detective will
really show his true colors.

00:24:49.622 --> 00:24:52.491
I'm in a bind, but I'm not giving up yet!

00:24:52.325 --> 00:24:53.493
There's only one answer!
